3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: android-tester
tools: adb, sh
persona: drives a real Android emulator via adb — first real (non-guidance) pass at this target
---
Test agent for the Android target. Previously guidance-only (no `adb` or
emulator in the interactive dev sandbox this was first written in) — this
is the first real pass, proven via CI where
`reactivecircus/android-emulator-runner` provides an actual booted
emulator. That action owns the emulator's own lifecycle (boot, shutdown)
for the duration of one step; unlike specs/ios.3md there's no separate
boot/shutdown skill here, because the emulator only exists inside that
one step, not across the whole job.

@plane z=0 label="android-tester" kind=identity

# android-tester

Assume a booted emulator already exists — the caller's job is responsible
for that. Just prove `adb` can see it and pull real evidence back.

@plane z=1 label="devices" kind=skill triggers="devices, adb, list, connected" tool="adb devices"

# Skill: devices

Lists connected devices/emulators. Proves `adb` can see a live emulator
before trying anything else with it.

@plane z=2 label="screenshot" kind=skill triggers="screenshot, snapshot, capture, image" tool="sh scripts/android-screenshot.sh artifacts/android/screenshot.png"

# Skill: screenshot

`adb exec-out screencap` writes binary PNG data — needs a real file
redirect, not this engine's own text-based stdout capture, hence the
wrapper script. Requires [[z=1|devices]].

@plane z=3 label="record" kind=skill triggers="video, record, recording, screen capture" tool="sh scripts/android-record.sh artifacts/android/recording.mp4 3"

# Skill: record

Records on-device via `adb shell screenrecord`, then pulls the file back
to the host. Requires [[z=1|devices]].
